course: dictionary
lesson: 10268
title: Toothpaste and clean teeth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Toothpaste is a soft paste that you put on a toothbrush to clean your teeth. A dictionary tells you what a word means, and the sentences around it show you how it is used. Read the words around a new word to find its meaning.
explain: «Brush twice a day for about two minutes with fluoride toothpaste.» Brush means to clean with a brush, and the words around it tell you when and how long to do it. Fluoride is a special ingredient in the toothpaste that helps your teeth.
explain: «Never put butter, toothpaste or ice on a burn, because they can make it worse or cause infection.» The word never is a clue. It tells you that toothpaste is not for burns, even though it is used for teeth. The same word can be useful in one place and wrong in another.
explain: Toothpaste is a paste, so it is a thick, soft mixture. «Toothpaste and ketchup are fine solid bits in a liquid; they sit still until pushed hard enough, then flow.» The sentence helps you picture how a paste can stay still and then move when you squeeze it.
fact: Toothpaste is a soft paste that you put on a toothbrush.
fact: You should brush your teeth twice a day for about two minutes.
fact: Fluoride toothpaste makes teeth strong and helps stop holes called cavities.
fact: Use only a small, pea-sized amount, and spit it out instead of swallowing it.
fact: «Toothpaste» is uncountable, so you say some toothpaste, not a toothpaste, unless you mean a type or a tube.
exercise: «Brush twice a day for about two minutes with fluoride toothpaste.» What does fluoride toothpaste do for your teeth? | Turns them white in one day | Makes them soft and sticky | Stops them growing | *Makes them strong and helps stop holes
exercise: «Toothpaste and ketchup are fine solid bits in a liquid; they sit still until pushed hard enough, then flow.» What does flow mean? | Stay still | Break into pieces | *Move smoothly, like a liquid | Turn into a solid
exercise: «Never put butter, toothpaste or ice on a burn.» Why should you never put toothpaste on a burn? | It makes the burn feel sweet | It helps the burn heal faster | *It can make the burn worse or cause infection | It cools the burn straight away
test:  How long should you brush your teeth? | *About two minutes | Half an hour | One minute | Ten seconds
test: After brushing, what should you do with the toothpaste? | Keep it in your mouth all night | Eat it with your breakfast | Swallow it to keep the fluoride in | *Spit it out, do not swallow it
exam: Which is the best way to get toothpaste out of a «tube of toothpaste»? | Shake the tube hard | *Squeeze it from the bottom | Cut the tube open with scissors | Squeeze it from the middle
